  "uv": "Water pieces carry their own UVs (not palette cells): a box projection in studs from the asset origin, one texture tile per tile_studs. Up-facing faces: u = X / tile, v = Z / tile (mod 1, Roblox axes); faces toward +-Z use (X, -Y), toward +-X use (-Z, -Y). Set MeshPart.TextureID to the uploaded texture (it wraps), Transparency from the piece, Material SmoothPlastic, CastShadow false. Assets placed on a tile_studs grid continue the pattern seamlessly.",
  "flow": "Pieces of an asset with a water_flow socket carry flow = {direction (unit, Roblox X/Z), speed (studs/s), socket}. To animate, use a Texture (Face Top, StudsPerTileU/V = tile_studs) on the piece instead of TextureID and move OffsetStudsU/V along direction * speed each frame."
